<title>UK: UK bookmakers cut Labour's odds to 18-year low.</title>
<headline>UK bookmakers cut Labour's odds to 18-year low.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bookmakers William Hill said on Wednesday they had cut the odds on the main opposition Labour party winning the election to 1-6, the lowest since it lost power to the Conservatives in 1979.</p>
<p>Labour's odds were cut from 1-5. The Conservatives are quoted at 7-2. A hung parliament where no party has an overall majority was quoted at 3-1.</p>
<p>The election must be held by May 22 and May 1 is strong favourite.</p>
</text>
